Helpers the traits and the rest of the library share, internal to ca:

- `is_any_of<T, Ts...>`: T is one of Ts, the concept behind every closed list of types
  (`is_character`, the unsigned types of `bit/`).
- `copy_cv<From, To>`: To with the const and volatile qualifiers of From, for accessors that
  return a member with the constness of the object.
- `is_referenceable<T>`: whether `T&` is a valid type (not void, not an abominable function
  type), the guard of `add_lvalue_reference` and `add_rvalue_reference`.

```c++
#include "1-primitives/traits/impl/copy_cv.hpp"
#include "1-primitives/traits/impl/is_any_of.hpp"
#include "1-primitives/traits/is_same.hpp"

static_assert(ca::impl::is_any_of<int, char, int, long>);
static_assert(ca::is_same<ca::impl::copy_cv<const int, long>, const long>);
```
